    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "Solve $9^x-3^{x+1}+2=0$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=0$ or $x=\\log_3(2)$.\n\nRewrite as a quadratic in $3^x$ and factor.",
      "worked": "Since $9^x=(3^x)^2$ and $3^{x+1}=3(3^x)$,\n$$\\begin{align*}(3^x)^2-3(3^x)+2&=0\\\\(3^x-1)(3^x-2)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus either\n$$\\begin{align*}3^x&=1\\\\x&=0,\\end{align*}$$\nor\n$$\\begin{align*}3^x&=2\\\\x&=\\log_3(2).\\end{align*}$$\nBoth exponential values are positive, so both solutions are valid.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
